  contents: [{'_map_index': 0, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/statemachine-engine", "number": 1, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/statemachine-engine/pull/1", "title": "fix(engine): idle-tick precedence \\u2014 only \'waiting\' selects 500ms tick (FR-FSM-019) v1.0.91", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T02:21:32Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T02:25:58Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "## FR-FSM-019\\n\\n`is_idle` in `execute_state_machine()` mixed `and`/`or` without parentheses; the stale-activity disjunct ignored `current_state`, so any machine quiet >5s polled its control socket at 500ms in every state.\\n\\nNow: `waiting AND (no activity OR stale activity)`. Present since initial commit `6a97041`; the code comment already stated the intended semantics.\\n\\n### Measured (real control socket, state `listening`, activity aged 10s, 40 sends)\\n\\n| | p50 | p90 | max |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| before | 216 ms | 454 ms | 476 ms |\\n| after | 18 ms | 27 ms | 33 ms |\\n\\n### Commits\\n- RED `fd0b9ca` \\u2014 `tests/core/test_idle_tick_precedence.py` (fails `0.5 == 0.05` pre-fix)\\n- GREEN `d95b1ed` \\u2014 parenthesise expression\\n- chore \\u2014 v1.0.91, CHANGELOG, FR status\\n- measurement script `tmp/fr019_latency.py`\\n\\nFull suite: 416 passed / 9 skipped. ruff clean.", "additions": 225, "deletions": 16, "changed_files": 7, "base_sha": "377005db637ee8bfad3f282005ae04a1c52e925e", "head_sha": "5f52d617e2cb3a9180c6d8935c6b56b47a5d713b"}'}, {'_map_index': 1, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/yamlgraph", "number": 577, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/yamlgraph/pull/577", "title": "feat(judge): FR-960 Claude judge variant - judge_claude node, JUDGE_BACKEND selection, per-backend-per-FR artifact", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T02:32:25Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T03:38:52Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nEnforces FR-960 (child D-2 of the FR-958 SPLIT): an opt-in Claude Code judge node inside the sole-route judge graph, selected by `JUDGE_BACKEND=claude scripts/judge.sh <fr>`, plus a per-backend-per-FR artifact name that ends the fixed-name clobber.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Judgement:** [FR-960 judgement](feature-requests/FR-960-claude-judge-variant.judgement.md) \\u2014 APPROVED WITH REVISIONS via the sole route; R-1..R-6 folded. Gate C-2 (FR-959 on main) satisfied by #563.\\r\\n- **Graph authoring route:** graph + prompt edited only by `scripts/author.sh` from the committed [brief](feature-requests/authoring-briefs/fr-960-claude-judge-variant-brief.md); report digest and quoted sections in the witness.\\r\\n- **Witness:** [FR-960-claude-judge-witness.md](feature-requests/evidence/FR-960-claude-judge-witness.md) \\u2014 Copilot and Claude judge runs on FR-961, AC-13 invalid-key run, R-6 claim inventory (11 matched / 4 contradicted / 7 backend-only; the Claude judge found an allow-path auto-approve risk the Copilot judge missed). C-8 signed by the spend owner.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n- `.github/skills/judge-fr/adapters/graph.yaml`, `prompts/judge.yaml`: `select` passthrough, state-conditioned edges, `judge_claude` (`backend: claude`, `tools`/`allowed_tools` = Read,Glob,Grep,Write, `max_turns: 40`, no bypass); prompt writes to `{{ artifact_path }}`. Copilot node unchanged except the added variable.\\r\\n- `scripts/judge.sh`: `JUDGE_BACKEND` validated before the lock (exit 64 otherwise); artifact `tmp/draft-judgement-<backend>-<fr-slug>.md`; `--var backend/artifact_path`.\\r\\n- `adapters/README.md`, `SKILL.md`: two backend nodes, one route; overwrite rule; four-tool boundary; payer link to FR-959.\\r\\n- CAP-211: REQ-YG-642; REQ-YG-632 re-scoped (one Copilot-CLI node pinned, every copilot node pinned); `ARCHITECTURE.md` regenerated; changelog fragment; diary.\\r\\n- Tests: `tests/unit/test_fr960_claude_judge_variant.py` (8 stubbed wrapper + 4 mocked routing, REQ-YG-642), `test_fr931` re-scoped, FR-758 judge stubs use the new artifact name.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- RED then GREEN commits. Routing + pin tests 7 passed; `yamlgraph graph lint` 0 issues; `graph validate` ok; `req_coverage --strict`, `validate_capabilities --strict` pass.\\r\\n- The 26 bash wrapper tests (FR-758 + FR-960) cannot spawn `bash` from pytest on the Windows host (FR-953 class) \\u2014 exercised by hand under Git Bash with the same stub (all five behaviours), and run by CI here.\\r\\n- Live: three judge runs on FR-961 through the new wrapper (Copilot; Claude; Claude with invalid API key). Preflight `2.1.255` / `claude.ai` each time; both backends\' drafts coexist.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Human gates (FR-960 AC-16)\\r\\n\\r\\n- Signature 2 (C-8, spend for judge execution): **recorded** \\u2014 sheikkinen, 2026-09-03.\\r\\n- Signature 1 (C-7, infrastructure diff and route invariants): **pending your review of this PR**. FR-960 moves to Implemented when it is written into the witness \\u00a74.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Review (sole route, scripts/review.sh on head 96770e44)\\r\\n\\r\\nNot approved with P1-P3. *", "additions": 1433, "deletions": 43, "changed_files": 19, "base_sha": "639754309669082726dde7f4871676acb98dd729", "head_sha": "3d5891cc84f4e348b2696296f2be4fb70dce4740"}'}, {'_map_index': 2, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/yamlgraph", "number": 578, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/yamlgraph/pull/578", "title": "docs(reference): index the schema-driven-extraction pattern", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T02:43:01Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T02:44:45Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "## What\\r\\n\\r\\n`reference/patterns/schema-driven-extraction.md` shipped with FR-467 and has been\\r\\nupdated twice since, but never got a row in the reference index. It was the only\\r\\npattern in `reference/patterns/` unreachable from `reference/README.md`.\\r\\n\\r\\nFound while auditing inbound links to the coded-classification pattern.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Scope\\r\\n\\r\\nOne table row. Docs only.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo generated artifact is affected: FR-855 would generate `reference/pattern-index.md`\\r\\nfrom `examples/**/graph.yaml` (keyed node type -> example path), which is a different\\r\\nfile from this hand-maintained concept -> doc table. The two cannot clobber each other.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Follow-up worth considering (not in this PR)\\r\\n\\r\\nNothing drift-checks that every `reference/patterns/*.md` is reachable from\\r\\n`reference/README.md`. That is the general fix; this PR is the instance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n", "additions": 1, "deletions": 0, "changed_files": 1, "base_sha": "9e6b3335d33ee80b13b175c8d50d82732a292fda", "head_sha": "2031653169e092d54d2b48a5770a24e797618846"}'}, {'_map_index': 3, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/yamlgraph", "number": 579, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/yamlgraph/pull/579", "title": "docs(research): coded-classification use-case screen and candidate research", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T02:43:08Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T02:57:36Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "## What\\r\\n\\r\\nA research document screening the vocabulary space reachable by the\\r\\ncoded-classification pattern (`reference/patterns/coded-classification.md`), asking\\r\\nwhich candidates would teach the pattern something its two instances did not.\\r\\n\\r\\nComplements `docs/2026-09-02-brainstorm-business-use-cases.md`, which ranked the same\\r\\nterritory commercially. This document deliberately does not re-rank it - it sorts by\\r\\nresearch yield instead, which reorders almost everything.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Contents\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Three gates the pattern doc does not state:** G4 gold economics, G5 rule surface,\\r\\n  G6 item independence.\\r\\n- **Two pattern shapes:** vocabulary crosswalk (code -> code) and temporal recoding\\r\\n  (version bump). Both self-labeling; both asserted, not demonstrated.\\r\\n- **Ten screened candidates**, including instructive failures recorded so they are not\\r\\n  re-proposed (CPV fails G1 on title-only rubrics; SNOMED CT full fails G2).\\r\\n- **Nine research questions**, each naming the candidate that would settle it.\\r\\n- **A consolidated list of six law amendments** the candidates would force, with the\\r\\n  three that cost nothing to adopt separated from the three that need an instance.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Notable findings\\r\\n\\r\\n- A statute (**MDR Annex VIII** - 22 rules in 4 groups, \\"strictest rule governs\\")\\r\\n  and a game rulebook (**D&D SRD 5.1/5.2**, CC-BY-4.0) outrank six carefully screened\\r\\n  taxonomies. Both ship an adjudication procedure rather than just labels, which is\\r\\n  what law 5 says pays best - and neither was on the pattern doc\'s \\"fits\\" list.\\r\\n- **MTG passes every stated prerequisite and fails an unstated one.** Item\\r\\n  independence is listed first in the 09-02 doc\'s map-reduce reflection but is absent\\r\\n  from the pattern\'s three prerequisites, because both instances satisfy it by\\r\\n  accident. MTG is the worked negative example the \\"what does not transfer\\" section\\r\\n  lacks.\\r\\n- **Law 1\'s \\"never committed\\" half is licensing-contingent**, not universal. Wizards\\r\\n  supplies both poles: D&D SRD is CC-BY committable, MTG\'s Fan Content Policy forbids\\r\\n  redistribution. Same machinery, opposite obligations.\\r\\n- **OIICS** is the only candidate offering an external accuracy comparison (229,820\\r\\n  labeled records, 48 codes in 7 clusters, published SOTA 81->89%). Both current\\r\\n  instances report agreement, and the pattern doc itself warns that agreement is not\\r\\n  accuracy.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Status\\r\\n\\r\\nResearch only. No FR is authorized and no implementation is proposed.\\r\\n\\r\\nExternal claims are cited in a Sources section. Load-bearing assumptions that were\\r\\n**not** verified are marked as such - notably EUDAMED as a gold source, which decides\\r\\nwhether the rank-1 candidate is buildable at all, and MTG Comprehensive Rules\\r\\nnumbering.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\ud83e\\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n", "additions": 636, "deletions": 0, "changed_files": 1, "base_sha": "5580d65fbbe6bbd2203afe1ab3bc7b4b4fed02d5", "head_sha": "0e3ec52981fd8439cd92a13b159704cb78d8ffac"}'}, {'_map_index': 4, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/yamlgraph", "number": 580, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/yamlgraph/pull/580", "title": "docs(fr): FR-981 phased summary pattern - planning record, research and judgement", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T03:46:40Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T04:05:51Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "Planning-only record for FR-981. **No implementation** \\u2014 the demo, graph,\\nprompts, tests, and the pattern document are all deliverables of a later\\nchange, and the judgement\'s authority is inactive pending human review (C-1).\\n\\n## What is here\\n\\n- `FR-981-module-history-phased-summary-demo.md` \\u2014 the FR, with judgement\\n  revisions R-1..R-7 folded.\\n- `FR-981-module-history-phased-summary-demo.judgement.md` \\u2014 APPROVED WITH\\n  REVISIONS. Strategic classification: contrib/example with pattern\\n  documentation; no framework primitive, no new CAP/REQ.\\n- `FR-981.research.md` + `research-briefs/fr981-phased-summary-witness-brief.md`\\n  \\u2014 the FR-890 sole-route research record (five personas) and its closed brief.\\n- `FR-981-pilot-raw-read.md` \\u2014 the pre-authority raw read required by R-6.\\n\\n## The pattern\\n\\nLong records about one subject are reduced to durable typed briefs; the\\nsubject\'s rollup reads briefs only; a new record costs one brief. Externally\\nthis is CLIN-SUMM (medRxiv preprint) with POMR (Weed, 1964) as its ancestor \\u2014\\nso the *shape* needs no witness from this repository. What is unexercised is\\nthe YAMLGraph composition, which is what the proposed demo would witness.\\n\\n## Two things worth reading\\n\\n**The research route dissented against the first draft.** Three of five\\npersonas dissented and the only in-repo `pursue` was to withdraw the pattern\\ndocumentation entirely. That argument rested on \\"a single unverifiable\\nanecdote\\" \\u2014 a premise the librarian\'s external precedent removed, since\\npersonas run in parallel and could not see each other. The dissent is\\npreserved rather than resolved away, and the subtractionist\'s principle\\nsurvives as a standing condition: the pattern document must keep its\\nUNEXERCISED grade if the demo is never built.\\n\\n**The pilot read changed the design three times.** Reading three real commit\\ndiffs against three hand-authored briefs showed the schema dropping an\\ninverted latency measurement, an operational 500-on-temperature trap, and a\\nsecond FR bundled into one commit. The `salient_other` cap, the\\n`paths_changed_count` field, and multi-reference `why` all exist because of\\nthat read, not because of design.\\n\\n## Known gap\\n\\n`--verify-promotion` reports `mismatched` on the research record. This is a\\nrepository-wide newline defect, not this FR\'s: `research.sh` hashes raw CRLF\\nbytes while the verifier hashes LF-normalized text, and the committed,\\nenforced FR-955 record reports the same today. `--verify-artifact` passes, so\\nthe content is verified. A separate FR is owed for the newline boundary; the\\nalternative \\u2014 rewriting the recorded digest to make a verifier pass \\u2014 was\\nrejected as falsifying the launcher\'s attestation.\\n\\n\\ud83e\\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n", "additions": 961, "deletions": 0, "changed_files": 6, "base_sha": "e02fe6943d3d02c853005718ce74fa804a91d200", "head_sha": "d7a6f6490614dd2ddd48a9f65daf4ae4ebb4a2be"}'}, {'_map_index': 5, 'value': '{"repo": "sheikkinen/yamlgraph", "number": 581, "url": "https://github.com/sheikkinen/yamlgraph/pull/581", "title": "docs(fr): FR-981 amend store precedent and graph-boundary claim", "state": "merged", "created_at": "2026-09-04T04:38:13Z", "merged_at": "2026-09-04T04:48:22Z", "labels": [], "body_head": "Two factual corrections to FR-981, found after #580 merged, plus the research\\nrecord that produced the second one. No re-judgement: this corrects claims of\\nfact, does not widen scope, allocates no identifiers, and activates no\\nauthority. The judgement\'s gates C-1..C-8 stand.\\n\\n## Correction 1 \\u2014 the durable store is precedented twice, not zero times\\n\\nFR-981 claimed the store, the invalidation rule, and the \\"every claim resolves\\nto a stored artifact\\" gate were \\"precedented zero times\\". Two committed graphs\\nsay otherwise:\\n\\n- `examples/demos/wiki-memory` (CAP-173/174) \\u2014 `wiki/<id>.yaml` per page via\\n  `write_data_file`, read back through a `data_files` glob on later runs,\\n  gated by a Python node that rejects unresolvable references.\\n- `examples/novel_fandom` (CAP-181) \\u2014 typed `canon/character/*.yaml` and\\n  `canon/event/*.yaml` under a no-orphan gate *and* lane immutability, which\\n  bars the model from overwriting `lane: static` pages.\\n\\nThe surviving novelty claim still justifies the demo: substitution, the\\nsubject-scoped rollup, version-keyed invalidation, and counted incremental\\ncost remain unexercised. The store and the reference gate do not.\\n\\n## Correction 2 \\u2014 \\"the store is not a graph\\" is withdrawn\\n\\nFR-981 concluded *\\"the phases are; the store is not\\"*, on four of five\\nresearch rows answering `is_this_a_graph: No`. A second sole-route run,\\npointed at the two witnesses above, returned four of five answering **Yes** \\u2014\\n`write_data_file` persists the keyed artifact, `data_files` reads it back, and\\nthe gates are `type: python` nodes *inside* the graph.\\n\\nThe difference is method, not opinion: the first route reasoned about the\\nframework in the abstract, the second read graphs that already do it.\\n\\nThe claim is withdrawn as overstated rather than replaced, because the frozen\\n`plan_briefs`/`persist` design rests on it. Enforcement owes a decision: if\\nthe store is expressible with `write_data_file` + `data_files`, return to Plan\\nfor a scope revision rather than hand-rolling persistence under a superseded\\npremise.\\n\\n## Also included\\n\\n- `docs/2026-09-04-research-durable-keyed-artifact-store.md` \\u2014 the FR-890\\n  sole-route record behind correction 2. Marked **pre-FR**: promotable to\\n  `FR-XXX.research.md` unchanged when the pattern FR is filed. 5/5 `pursue`.\\n  It rejects the librarian\'s Event Sourcing framing (these stores overwrite\\n  keyed current state; they keep no event log and replay nothing) and flags\\n  `FR-874` [REJECTED] as prior art the filing FR must disposition.\\n- The brief, and its `research-runs.jsonl` provenance line.\\n- A diary reflection. Both errors share one root: every search \\u2014 manual and\\n  mechanical \\u2014 was keyed on the vocabulary of summarisation, and the witnesses\\n  share the *problem* while sharing no word. Doctrine documents this about\\n  `prior_art.py`; I quoted that sentence into the FR while committing the\\n  error it describes.\\n\\n## Known gaps\\n\\n`--verify-promotion` reports `mismatched` on this host for any byte-faithful\\npromotion (launcher", "additions": 857, "deletions": 2, "changed_files": 7, "base_sha": "49ac494c5127d4b48f4a1e29aa039b110daa1ff2", "head_sha": "0eae0c73009b24b287e84a280500fd2dd377a821"}'}]
